“This is our resource-swap price” = the tour fee is pressed very low, and profit may come from shopping kickbacks or optional paid items;
“Zero coercion throughout the whole trip” = the contract may not state anything mandatory, but on-site they may use stay duration, wording, or atmosphere to pressure you;
“Upgraded experiences are voluntary” = the basic itinerary may be pretty thin, and the core experiences cost extra;
“Government-subsidized slots” = first ask the other party to produce verifiable subsidy documents, don’t just listen to verbal claims;
“Quality pure-fun borderline price” = the key is to check whether the contract clearly states the number of shopping stops, the optional-expense list, accommodation standards, and losses if you withdraw from the tour.
